cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PhyloProcessR in your research, please cite the software using these metadata."
type: software
title: "PhyloProcessR: A Modular Toolkit for Targeted Sequence-Capture Phylogenomics"
authors:
  - family-names: Hutter
    given-names: Carl
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6381-6339"
version: 1.0.0
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/PhyloForge/PhyloProcessR"
url: "https://github.com/PhyloForge/PhyloProcessR"
keywords:
  - phylogenomics
  - sequence capture
  - targeted sequencing
  - bioinformatics
  - R
abstract: >-
  A modular R toolkit for processing targeted sequence-capture data from raw
  reads to curated, analysis-ready phylogenomic datasets. Functions can be
  called independently or combined into supplied or project-specific
  workflows.
